cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  AllelePerturb: measurement-resolution diagnostics for single-cell
  perturbation benchmarks
message: >-
  If you use this software or the benchmark, please cite the article below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Bo
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Artificial Intelligence, University of Macau
repository-code: https://github.com/Boom5426/AllelePerturb
license: MIT
keywords:
  - single-cell
  - perturbation prediction
  - benchmark
  - measurement resolution
  - protein-coding variants
abstract: >-
  A benchmark whose ground truth cannot separate two perturbations cannot order
  two models that differ in how well they separate them, so its ranking reports
  the measurement as much as the methods. AllelePerturb measures that property
  of a dataset before any model is trained, and applies it to allele-resolution
  single-cell perturbation prediction across 470 protein-coding variants and
  321,043 cells.
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    Measurement and model limits of allele-specific single-cell perturbation
    prediction
  authors:
    - family-names: Li
      given-names: Bo
      affiliation: >-
        Department of Artificial Intelligence, University of Macau
  year: 2026
  notes: Manuscript in preparation
